[{:seon.task/name "a-dependency-is-fetched-through-its-owner"
  :seon.task/plan "The PKG plan's Seon side, step one (`/Users/sean/src/seon-jolt/notes/option3-PKG-plan.md`, owner-approved 2026-10-21): fetching a dependency is an outside-world effect, so it goes through the effect owner like file write-back and git (`seon.fx/write-file`, `seon.fx/git-commit`; DECISIONS \"Loading code is an effect\"). Add a `:deps` effect kind whose performer `seon.fx/resolve-deps` takes `{:req {:deps <a deps.edn :deps map>}}`, resolves it with Jolt's own `jolt.deps/resolve-deps` (no resolver of ours: Jolt already fetches `:mvn/version` and `:git/sha`, uses `:local/root`, and caches in `.cpcache`), and answers `{:value {:roots [absolute source roots]}}` or its one typed error `:seon.fx/unresolved` naming the deps that did not resolve. Declare the kind beside the others in `seon.fx` (its workers and the system declaration as the existing kinds are), document the error in `docs/DRAGONS.md`, and the kind in the wiki section where effects live. Needs J1 (`jolt.ns/a-built-binary-requires-a-stdlib-namespace-it-did-not-compile`) landed first, so a root and an agent can then require what was resolved. Done by session DEPS (2026-10-21): `seon.fx/resolve-deps`, `:deps` in `seon.fx/kinds` and `resources/seon/system.edn`, `:seon.fx/unresolved` in `seon.problems.edn`. Learned: `jolt.deps/resolve-deps` throws `{:unresolved [{:coord :version :detail}]}` for a missing :mvn/version or git dep, but answers a `:local/root` that does not exist as a root (`manifest-info` never checks), so the performer checks :libs' local roots itself until `jolt.deps/a-missing-local-root-is-unresolved` moves that into Jolt. Measured (fresh HOME, niced): :mvn/version camel-snake-kebab 0.4.3 cold 433 ms (one POM and jar over HTTPS), warm 1 ms; :git/sha medley cold 1433 ms (clone), warm 0 ms; missing coordinate answered in 440 ms. Not in this task: `add-deps` and `sync-deps` at the REPL (J2) and checksums (J3)."
